Stop [E3001]: `panic: one is not two`
  --> test_members.jet:20 in __test_expect_fail region must fail
     |
20 |         assert((1 == 2), "one is not two")
     |         ^^^^^^
 Why: The program hit a `panic`, `assert`, or `assert_eq` call that failed, a bounds/key check triggered at runtime, or another program-side stop. The shared report boundary owns the program-side stop; an unhandled entry error is a returned report, not E3001. Jet file and line are shown in Jet terms — never generated-Rust terms (I2).
 Fix: Fix the logic that led to the failure. Program-side stops exit 70 through the shared boundary; unhandled entry errors print their report and exit 1; exit 101 is reserved for Jet defects.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3001

